<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sierra Leone</h1><p class="st-meta">1961 CE – present · capital Freetown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A West African republic, independent from Britain in 1961, with a one-party era, an eleven-year civil war to 2002 and multi-party elections since 2007.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate">Sierra Leone Colony and Protectorate</a> became independent on 27 April 1961 under Prime Minister Sir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-margai">Milton Margai</a> of the Sierra Leone People's Party. It remained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> with Queen Elizabeth as head of state, and adopted a republican constitution in 1971.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Margai's brother Albert succeeded him in 1964. Siaka Stevens of the All People's Congress won the 1967 election and was ousted by a coup within hours, but returned to power in 1968 after a second coup. He became president in 1971 and in 1978 made the APC the only legal party. Joseph Saidu Momoh succeeded him in 1985. In 1991 a constitution restored multi-party politics, and the same year a civil war began between the government and the Revolutionary United Front. About 50,000 people were killed between 1991 and 2001.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The war ended in January 2002 after intervention by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecomog">ECOMOG</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> and British forces. Ahmad Tejan Kabbah was re-elected in May 2002, and elections in 2007 and 2012 returned multi-party democracy. An Ebola epidemic in 2014 led to a national state of emergency. Julius Maada Bio became president after the March 2018 election.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sierra-leone.jpg" alt="Sierra Leone" width="330" height="220"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sierra_Leone.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1961 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Freetown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Milton Margai, Albert Margai, Siaka Stevens, Joseph Saidu Momoh, Ahmad Tejan Kabbah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Christianity, traditional African religions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Krio</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Sierra Leone</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1994&amp;focus=sierra-leone" aria-label="Sierra Leone on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4314 1861 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sierra Leone lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4634 2117L4634 2117"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4634 2117h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4634 2117h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4634 2117h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Freetown. <a href="/atlas?year=1994&amp;focus=sierra-leone">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
